G3306.def:
μένω, 
[in LXX for קוּם ,עמד, etc. ;] 
to stay, abide, remain. 
__1. Intrans.; 
__(i) of place: before ἐν, Luc 8:27, al.; παρά, with dative of person(s), Jean 1:40, al; σύν, Luc 1:56; καθ᾽ ἑαυτόν, Actes 28:16; with adv., ἐκεῖ, Matthieu 10:11; ὧδε, Matthieu 26:38; metaphorically, 1 Jean 2:18; of the Holy Spirit, Jean 1:32, 33 14:17; of Christ, Jean 6:56 15:4, al.; ὁ θεός, 1 Jean 4:15, conversely, of Christians, Jean 6:56 15:4, 1 Jean 4:15, al.; ὁ λόγος τ. θεοῦ, 1 Jean 2:14; ἡ ἀλήθεια, II Jo 2, al. 
__(ii) Of time; 
__(a) of persons: Philippiens 1:25; before εἰς τ. αἰῶνα, Jean 12:34, Hébreux 7:24, 1 Jean 2:17; ὀλίγον, Apocalypse 17:10; ἕως ἔρχομαι, Jean 21:22, 23; 
__(b) of things, lasting or enduring: cities, Matthieu 11:23, Hébreux 13:14; λόγος θεοῦ, 1 Pierre 1:23; ἁμαρτία, Jean 9:41. 
__(iii) Of condition: with pred., μόνος, Jean 12:24; ἄγαμος, 1 Corinthiens 7:11; πιστός, 2 Timothée 2:13; ἱερεύς, Hébreux 7:3; with adv., οὕτως, 1 Corinthiens 7:40; ὡς κἀγώ, ib. 8; before ἐν, ib. 20, 24. 
__2. Trans. (Bl., §34, 1; Field, Notes, 132): with accusative of person(s), Actes 20:5, 23 (cf. ἀνα-, δια-, ἐν-, ἐπι-, κατα-, παρα-, συν-παρα-, περι-, προσ-, ὑπο-μένω).

G3307.def:
μερίζω
(μέρος), [in LXX chiefly for חָלַק ;] 
to divide; 
__(a) to divide into parts : metaphorically, pass., 1 Corinthiens 7:34 (WH, R, ing.), 1 Corinthiens 7:34 (Rec., R, txt.) ( reading and punctuation, see ICC, in l); μεμέρισται ὁ Χριστός, 1 Corinthiens 1:13; as in late authors, of factional division (cf. Polyb., viii, 23, 9), καθ᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, Matthieu 12:25; ἐφ᾽ εαυτόν, Matthieu 12:26, Marc 3:24-26; 
__(b) to distribute: with accusative of thing(s) and dative of person(s), Marc 6:41; as in later usage (cf. Polyb., xi, 28, 9), to bestow: Romains 12:3, 1 Corinthiens 7:17, 2 Corinthiens 10:13, Hébreux 7:2; mid., with accusative of thing(s) before μετά, Luc 12:13 (cf. δια-, συμ-μερίζω).†

G3342.def:
μεταξύ
(μετά + ξύν = σύν), [in LXX: Genèse 31:50, Juges 5:27, III Ki 15:6; 3Ki.15:32, Wis.4:10 16:19 18:23 * ;] 
__1. adv. of place and time (in NT time only); 
__(a) between: ἐν τῷ μ. (s.with χρόνῳ), Jean 4:31; 
__(b) in late writers (FlJ, Plut., al.), like μετά (adv.), after, afterwards: τὸ μ. σάββατον, Actes 13:42 (cf. Cl., Ro., I Co., 44, 2). 
__2. Prep. with genitive, between: of place, Matthieu 23:35, Luc 11:51 16:26, Actes 12:6; of persons, as to mutual relation, Matthieu 18:15, Actes 15:9, Romains 2:1-29 15:1-33.†

G3358.def:
μέτρον, -ου, τό 
[in LXX chiefly for מִדָּה, also for אֵיפָה, etc. ;] 
__1. that which is used for measuring, a measure; 
__(a) a vessel: fig., Matthieu 23:32, Luc 6:38; ἐκ μ., by measure, Jean 3:34; 
__(b) a rod or rule: Apocalypse 21:15, 17; figuratively, Matthieu 7:2, Marc 4:24. 
__2. That which is measured, measure: with genitive of thing(s), Romains 12:3, 2 Corinthiens 10:13, Éphésiens 4:7, 13 4:16.†

G3360.def:
μέχρι
(bef. consonants, exc. Luc 16:16, μέχρι Ἰωάνου) and μέχρις (bef. vowels, Mk, Ga, ll. with, Hébreux 12:4; see Bl., § 5, 4) 
__1. as prep., with genitive, as far as, even to, until; 
__(a) of place: Romains 15:19; 
__(b) of time : Matthieu 11:23 13:30 28:15, Luc 16:16, Actes 10:30 20:7, Romains 5:14, 1 Timothée 6:14, Hébreux 3:6, 14 9:10; 
__(with) of measure or degree : Philippiens 2:8, 30, 2 Timothée 2:9, Hébreux 12:4 (μ. αἵματος, cf. 2Ma.13:14). 
__2. As conjunct. (as long as), until: Éphésiens 4:13; μ. οὗ (Thuc., iii, 28, but more frequently μ. ἄν see BI., § 65, 10), Marc 13:30, Galates 4:19 (μ. is prop, an adv., cf. Lat. usgue, before prep. or adv.; LS, see word, and cf. ἄχρι).†

G3392.def:
μιαίνω 
[in LXX chiefly for טָמֵא ;] 
__1. to dye or stain. 
__2. to stain, defile, soil; 
__(a) in physical sense; 
__(b) in moral sense : Tite 1:15, Hébreux 12:15, Ju 8; 
__(with) in ritual sense (cf. Lévitique 22:5, al.): Jean 18:28.†
SYN.: μολύνω, to besmear, which also differs from μ. in that it is never used, as μ. in its primary meaning, in an honourable sense (cf. Tr., Syn., § xxxi)

G3398.def:
μικρός, -ά, -όν 
[in LXX chiefly for קָטָן, מָעַט ;] 
small, little; 
__1. of persons; 
__(a) lit., of stature: Marc 15:40 (MM, iii, xvi; on the view that age is meant, see Deiss., BS, 144), Luc 19:3; οἱ μ., the little ones, Matthieu 18:6, 10 18:14, Marc 9:42; 
__(b) hence metaphorically, of rank or influence (cf. Dalman, Words, 113 f.) : Matthieu 10:42, Luc 17:2, Actes 8:10 26:22, Hébreux 8:11" (LXX), Apocalypse 11:18 13:16 19:5, 18 20:12; compar., -ότερος, Matthieu 11:11, Luc 7:28 9:48. 
__2. Of things; 
__(a) of size : Matthieu 13:32 Marc 4:31, Jacques 3:5; 
__(b) of quantity: Luc 12:32, 1 Corinthiens 5:6, Galates 5:9, Apocalypse 3:8; 
__(with) of time : Jean 7:33 12:35, Apocalypse 6:11 20:3. 
__3. Neut., μικρόν, used adverbially; 
__(a) of distance: Matthieu 26:39, Marc 14:35; 
__(b) of quantity: 2 Corinthiens 11:1 11:16; 
__(with) of time : Jean 13:33 14:19 16:16-19, Hébreux 10:37; μετὰ μ., Matthieu 26:73, Marc 14:70.†
